**Executable gate contract.** The compiled sibling gate snapshot is the resolved membership, prerequisites and selection contract. Check acceptance coverage against the immutable oracle; do not expand the roster from generic applicability rules.

**Authorized effects.** {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a slot's item is run through its own parameters: a real polarizer item's leakage passes crossed light", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-RUN-SLOT-ITEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a sample item is solved at its own thickness, as the item evaluator solves it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-RUN-SLOT-ITEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a dial-mounted item is run at the angle its reading draws", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-RUN-SLOT-ITEMS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S82-RUN-SLOT-ITEMS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}

**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`

**How to implement.** The run law reads the setup's slots: a slot holding an item is evaluated through that item's model and its own parameters (the S8.2 brief: 'S8.1's run law reads the setup's slots in light order'; 001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; the S8.1 mapper's request: Prep and Analyzer slots become `ElementStep`s and Object slots `ObjectStep`s through `ItemModelChoice.boundWith` / `BoundOpticalElement.muellerAt` at the slot's R1, its drawn incidence and its path branch). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `chartForRun` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun`, as step 252 left it): a path step's element whose `content` is `ItemInSlot (id, _)` is built from the item of that id in `kitItems`, its `tryItemModelChoice` (step 263) and `choice.boundWith model.materials (ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters)` (steps 245, 251), bound once per path step, and evaluated by `muellerAt` at each point exactly as step 252 evaluates a bound preset or sample: `{ rotation = its R1, or the swept x when its R1 is varied; incidence = its drawn incidence, or the swept x under VaryR2; branch = the path step's branch }` and the point's wavelength. It is an `ObjectStep` for a `Sample` slot and an `ElementStep` for any other. Its R1 is the drawn one, which a dial reading set (step 258's `drawnWith`). An evaluation error shows step 252's failure chart, `The run cannot be evaluated` with the error's `describe`, `SampleMaterialErr` keeping its own title; an item the kit lacks, or whose model does not resolve, shows that chart with the `describe` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming it (step 255). A slot of `EmptySlotContent` is built from its library binding exactly as step 252 builds it. (2) `model.objectIds` (step 254) answers the `Sample` slots that hold an item or are bound to a library sample, in table order, so a sample item is an object of the capture rule. (3) `chartForRun`'s no-analyzer check (`noPolarizerOnPath`) counts a polarizer slot that holds an item as a polarizer, and its 'nothing bound to the varied element' check passes a varied slot that holds an item. Each doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. Nothing else changes: with no item in any slot every chart is step 252's, so `FsxAcceptanceTests` and the chart classes run as they are. Tests, in `ExperimentControlsTests` (step 252), each over `initMain ()` with items added through `AddItem` (step 239) and put in slots through `AssignSlot` (step 263), at 600 nm with the seeded intensity detector: `a slot's item is run through its own parameters: a real polarizer item's leakage passes crossed light`: a linear polarizer at R1 0° bound to its preset in front of a second linear polarizer holding a real-LP item (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`, `ExtinctionRatioLeakage`) whose `extinctionRatio` is set to 0.01 (`SetParameterState`, step 240), the second varied over R1 0 … 180° in 5 points: each S₀ equals that of the item's `BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm` at the point's rotation applied to `Propagation.inputStokes IdealLinear (0°)` within 1e-12, and at 90° it is above 1e-4 while the same table with the preset in place of the item reads below 1e-12. `a sample item is solved at its own thickness, as the item evaluator solves it`: a sample holding a glass-plate item (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1) whose `substrate.thickness` is set to 2e-3 m, varied over R2 0 … 60° in 7 points with capture T: each S₀ equals that of `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample` over the item's values (step 249) on `BranchTransmitted` at the point's incidence, spin 0, applied to `Propagation.unpolarizedStokes`, within 1e-12. `a dial-mounted item is run at the angle its reading draws`: behind a first linear polarizer bound to its preset, a second polarizer at R1 30° holding a `DialMounted DialNegative` item of the linear-polarizer preset whose `dialZero` is 10° (so its reading is −20°, step 258) is recorded by `CreateSetup`; the item's `dialZero` is then set to 20° and the setup activated (`ActivateSetup`, step 260), which draws the second polarizer at R1 40°; the chart of a sweep of the first polarizer over R1 0 … 90° in 4 points equals, within 1e-12, that of a table whose second polarizer is the bare preset at R1 40°. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the run law reads the slots' items, `chartForRun` MUST evaluate a slot holding an item through the item's model and parameters at its drawn orientation, as an object for a sample slot, `model.objectIds` MUST count sample items, and every chart with no item MUST be unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a slot's item is run through its own parameters: a real polarizer item's leakage passes crossed light`, `a sample item is solved at its own thickness, as the item evaluator solves it` and `a dial-mounted item is run at the angle its reading draws`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
